freshroot (0.1.1~test9) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * 06_freshroot: per-snapshot submenus listing all compatible kernels,
    not just the newest. Snapshots with no matching kernel are skipped.
  * freshroot-update: hold kernel packages referenced by any existing
    snapshot before running apt, preventing autoremove from breaking
    older snapshots
  * BIND_MOUNTS now applied to the default update path (in addition to
    --shell and --provision)
  * Support local:// REPO scheme: skip git clone and run install.sh
    directly from a path inside the container (pair with BIND_MOUNTS
    to test uncommitted playbooks/scripts)

 -- Joshua <joshua@example.com>  Tue, 07 Apr 2026 15:00:00 -0400

freshroot (0.1.1~test8) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * 06_freshroot: match each snapshot to the newest kernel that has
    modules inside it; skip snapshots with no compatible kernel.
    Prevents kernel panic when booting old snapshots after kernel upgrades.
  * Snapshot history submenu now shows kernel version per entry
  * BIND_MOUNTS now applied to the default update path (in addition to
    --shell and --provision)
  * Support local:// REPO scheme: skip git clone and run install.sh
    directly from a path inside the container (pair with BIND_MOUNTS
    to test uncommitted playbooks/scripts)

 -- Joshua <joshua@example.com>  Tue, 07 Apr 2026 14:00:00 -0400

